    "body": "As i am looking for a good invoicing app (previously used siwapp), i stumpled upon invoice ninja, which really looks awesome (only a little sad that it doesn't use symfony, which is my favorite framework :smile: but as the two frameworks are quite connected, i hope it will be no problem to get started with laravel)) \n\nfor me it feels a little bit awkward to use a cloud service as pdf generation instance. \n\nespecially if i use the invoice system on local system only, which is not publicly available (what i prefer for an invoice system). \n\nas @hillelcoren wrote [here](https://github.com/invoiceninja/invoiceninja/issues/587#issuecomment-167955413):\n\n> for this to work your app instance must be publicly available\n\nthis is not really logic, if i have a public system, i don't require to send the pdfs to my users, they can login and view and download them there but if my system is not publicly available, i **must** attach the pdfs or else they can't read the invoice.\n\nfrom the security point of view, i really don't like to send sensible invoice data, which contains customer data, prices, vat ids, ... to a cloud service.  this is also the reason why i am looking for a self hosted invoicing system, like yours is.\n\ni would really love to see an option that i can choose to use the cloud service or a locally installed phantomjs \n- https://www.npmjs.com/package/phantomjs-prebuilt\n- http://phantomjs.org/download.html\n\nor by using php to create the pdf (i would prefer security over exact visual appearance of the pdf file (browser pdf vs attached pdf))\n- https://packagist.org/packages/mpdf/mpdf\n- https://packagist.org/packages/nitmedia/wkhtml2pdf\n- https://packagist.org/packages/spipu/html2pdf\n",
